From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz.majnert@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:14:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] interp: extend G76 with tapered threads and alternating
 infeed

Ported to v2.10.0-pre2, where G76 checks its synchronized feed against
the axis velocity limits and holds the spindle override for the cycle.
A tapered cycle now checks every synchronized move of every pass at the
lead it is commanded with: the drive line, the X-only feed in and the
angled move of an entry taper, and the angled move of an exit taper,
each with its own X and Z components and, in G96, its own smallest
radius.  Upstream's cylindrical checks are kept unchanged for a G76
without X.  The pass geometry is computed once and used both for the
checks and for the moves.  A D word in a block with both G96 and G76 is
reported as ambiguous before it is range-checked as an infeed mode.
tests/g76-tapered-pitch exercises the check on a simulated lathe.
